The animation model, OpenGL renderer, glyph atlas generation, and kana data
were adapted from glmatrix-rs 0.1.5 by Eriks Remess and contributors:
https://github.com/EriksRemess/glmatrix-rs

Source baseline: bfc66ad (local checkout, 2026-11-13).
The source package declares the MIT license and retains Jamie Zawinski's
GLMatrix copyright and permission notice, reproduced in LICENSE.

Original GLMatrix: Jamie Zawinski, XScreenSaver.
The upstream source reference is recorded by glmatrix-rs in its README.

This port replaces Wayland windowing with offscreen EGL rendering, extracts
the simulation tick from presentation, and adds terminal input, frame encoding,
Kitty animation transport, and headless snapshots.

src/kana.rs contains monochrome glyph masks rasterized from Noto Sans CJK
by glmatrix-rs. The Noto font notice and SIL Open Font License 1.1 accompany
these derived bitmap assets in licenses/OFL-1.1.txt.
